# Testing standards

- Prefer the existing `tsx --test` runner + `c8` coverage; do not migrate the suite to Jest unless explicitly requested.
- Never modify production source when asked to write tests; report blockers instead.
- Never write tests that hit real networks, real FFmpeg, or the production DB.
- Use `TEST_DATABASE_URL` / `.env.test` only; refuse URLs that look like production hosts.
- Load mocks via `--import ./tests/setup/load-env.mjs --import ./tests/setup/register-mocks.mjs`.
- Every test must be deterministic: freeze time, seed randomness, no `sleep()`.
- Use AAA structure (Arrange/Act/Assert) with a descriptive test name.
- Always include negative, boundary, and authorization cases — not just happy path.
- For multi-tenant features, always assert reseller data isolation.
- Assert DB state, not just HTTP status codes.
- Tests must clean up after themselves (transaction rollback or truncate).
- No snapshot tests for API responses that IPTV clients depend on — assert keys explicitly.
- Use factories from `tests/factories/` for admin, reseller, sub-reseller, line, bouquet, stream, series, EPG, MAG.
